@ref Dieu 126 (src:2722-2733)
GIVEN c IS A `The contract of an agent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 126: the agency contract states the essential contents` c MEANS
        c's `states the name and address of the agent`
    AND c's `states the name and head office address of the insurer, branch or mutual organisation`
    AND c's `states the rights and obligations of both sides`
    AND c's `states the content and scope of the agency`
    AND c's `states commission, bonus and support, if any`
    AND c's `states the term of the contract`
    AND c's `states the way of resolving disputes`

§§ `Dieu 127: principles of acting as an agent`

-- Dieu 127(1), first paragraph. V1: an individual may not at once be an agent of two insurers operating in the same
-- type of insurance, or of two mutual organisations. From V2 (Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(9)): an agent of a life insurer may
-- not be an agent of another life insurer; of a non-life insurer or foreign non-life branch, not of another such;
-- of a health insurer, not of another; of a mutual organisation, not of another. The two texts part for a life insurer
-- that also carries on health insurance (Dieu 63(3)(a)): V1 bars it from sharing an agent with a health insurer, V2 does not.
